8 Best Free AI Video Generators in 2026 | WaveSpeedAI Blog
  URL: https://wavespeed.ai/blog/posts/best-free-ai-video-generators-2026/
  The best free AI video generators in 2026, compared by free tier limits, quality, speed, and features. From Kling and WAN 2.7 to Sora 2 and Veo

  --- Content ---
  [← Blog](https://wavespeed.ai/blog/)
  
  ![8 Best Free AI Video Generators in 2026](https://static.wavespeed.ai/media/images/1775454352321281840_iOvFOX6f.png)
  
  AI video generation went from novelty to production tool in 2025. By 2026, several platforms offer genuinely usable free tiers — enough to create short clips for social media, test concepts, or prototype creative ideas without paying.
  
  Here are the 8 best free AI video generators in 2026.
  
  * * *
  
  ## 1\. WaveSpeedAI Video Generator
  
  [Try it free ->](https://wavespeed.ai/video-generator)
  
  WaveSpeedAI gives you access to every major video model — WAN 2.7, Sora 2, Veo 3.1, Kling, Vidu, HaiLuo, and more — through a single interface with free credits on signup. Text-to-video, image-to-video, and video-to-video all in one place.
  
  - **Free tier**: Free credits on signup
  - **Models**: WAN 2.7, Sora 2, Veo 3.1 Fast, Kling, Vidu, HaiLuo, LTX, and 30+ more
  - **Key feature**: Compare models side by side — find what works for your use case
  - **Max duration**: Up to 15s depending on model
  - **Best for**: Model comparison, production pipelines, API access
  
  Instead of signing up for 5 different platforms, test every model from one place and pay per use only when you need to scale.
  
  * * *
  
  ## 2\. Kling AI
  
  Kling consistently offers one of the most generous free tiers in AI video. The motion quality is excellent — smooth, physically plausible movement that holds up across the full clip.
  
  - **Free tier**: ~66 credits/day (several generations)
  - **Key feature**: Exceptional motion smoothness, character consistency
  - **Max duration**: Up to 10 seconds
  - **Resolution**: 720p (free), 1080p (paid)
  - **Limitations**: Queue times for free users, 1080p locked to paid
  - **Paid**: From $6/month
  
  * * *
  
  ## 3\. HaiLuo AI (MiniMax)
  
  Fast generation with good quality — HaiLuo is the quick-and-dirty option when you need a clip now, not in 2 minutes. Human movement and facial expressions are a particular strength.
  
  - **Free tier**: Several free generations per day
  - **Key feature**: Fast generation, strong human motion
  - **Max duration**: Up to 6 seconds
  - **Resolution**: 720p
  - **Limitations**: Shorter clips, watermark on free tier
  - **Paid**: From ~$10/month
  
  * * *
  
  ## 4\. Pika
  
  Pika carved out a niche with creative effects — crush, melt, inflate, explode. If you need stylized or exaggerated motion rather than photorealism, Pika is where to start.
  
  - **Free tier**: ~150 credits on signup + daily replenishment
  - **Key feature**: Pika Effects for creative/stylized motion
  - **Max duration**: 3-4 seconds
  - **Resolution**: Up to 1080p
  - **Limitations**: Short clips, limited daily credits
  - **Paid**: From $10/month
  
  * * *
  
  ## 5\. Sora (ChatGPT)
  
  OpenAI includes Sora access in free ChatGPT accounts with limited monthly generations. The quality is high — strong physics simulation and cinematic camera work — but the free allowance is very small.
  
  - **Free tier**: Limited monthly generations (free ChatGPT)
  - **Key feature**: Best physics simulation, cinematic quality
  - **Max duration**: Up to 20 seconds
  - **Resolution**: Up to 1080p
  - **Limitations**: Very few free generations, slow queue
  - **Paid**: ChatGPT Plus ($20/month) for higher limits
  
  * * *
  
  ## 6\. WAN (Open Source)
  
  Alibaba’s WAN models are open-source and free to run locally. If you have the GPU (24GB+ VRAM for WAN 2.1/2.6), this is unlimited free video generation with competitive quality.
  
  - **Free tier**: Unlimited (self-hosted)
  - **Key feature**: Open-weight, no usage caps, community ecosystem
  - **Max duration**: 5-15 seconds depending on version
  - **Resolution**: Up to 720p (locally)
  - **Limitations**: Requires significant GPU; older versions lack WAN 2.7’s features
  - **Paid**: Free locally; WAN 2.7 via WaveSpeedAI for cloud access
  
  * * *
  
  ## 7\. LTX Video (Open Source)
  
  Lightricks’ LTX Video is open-source and optimized for speed. Not the highest quality in the group, but fast enough for rapid prototyping and concept testing.
  
  - **Free tier**: Unlimited (self-hosted)
  - **Key feature**: Fast generation, lightweight model
  - **Max duration**: ~5 seconds
  - **Resolution**: 720p
  - **Limitations**: Quality below commercial models
  - **Paid**: Free locally; hosted via various platforms
  
  * * *
  
  ## 8\. Vidu
  
  Vidu offers competitive quality with good character consistency features. The free tier is limited but enough to test the model and see if it fits your workflow.
  
  - **Free tier**: Limited credits on signup
  - **Key feature**: Character consistency, good general quality
  - **Max duration**: Up to 8 seconds
  - **Resolution**: Up to 1080p
  - **Limitations**: Smaller community, limited documentation
  - **Paid**: Credit-based pricing
  
  * * *
  
