  ## ➥ AI Video Generator Pricing
  
  Pricing matters because the best AI video generators often become expensive once you iterate for perfect motion, camera, and audio. Most AI video generators operate on a credit-based system or a monthly subscription. Here is the general breakdown.
  
  - **Freemium Plans:** Many tools give you a few free credits daily. This is great for testing the waters. You usually get watermarked videos.
  - **Subscription Tiers:** Monthly plans range from $12 to $100. These plans unlock higher resolution (1080p or 4K), remove watermarks, and give you faster generation times.
  - **Credit Packs:** Some platforms let you buy credits as you go. This is ideal if your volume fluctuates. High-quality generations usually cost more credits.
  
  ## ➥ Alternatives to AI Video Generators
  
  If you can’t get what you want with the best AI video generator, these alternatives can be better depending on your production needs. While AI video is amazing, sometimes you might want different tools. Here are some related categories to consider.
  
  ### AI Avatar Generators
  
  Tools like [HeyGen](https://www.aixploria.com/en/heygen-ai/ "HeyGen AI Avatar Video") or Synthesia focus on talking heads. If you want a spokesperson for training videos, these are better suited than general video generators. They provide perfect lip-syncing.
  
  ### Stock Footage Libraries
  
  Sites like Storyblocks or Shutterstock provide real-world footage. Sometimes real human emotion or specific real-world locations are unmatched by AI. They are reliable for corporate documentaries.
  
  ### Traditional Animation Software
  
  Software like After Effects gives you pixel-perfect control. AI can be random at times. If you want exact brand compliance and specific animations, manual tools are still king.
  
  ## ➥ Conclusion: Which AI Video Generator Should You Use?
  
  The "Best AI Video Generator" for you depends entirely on your deadline and your quality bar. Want Hollywood-level texture and motion? **Kling** or **Runway** are your best bets. Just want to make a funny clip for Twitter in 30 seconds? **Luma** is your friend.
  
  The technology is moving fast. What we wrote today might be upgraded by tomorrow morning. The only way to really get it? Get your hands dirty. Go grab some free credits, type in a crazy prompt, and see what happens. You might just create your next masterpiece.
  
  ## ➥ FAQ: Frequently Asked Questions
  
  ### What is the best free AI video generator? +
  
  Most tools operate on a "freemium" model. **Hailuo AI** and **Luma Dream Machine** currently provide generous free daily tiers or trial credits. However, for watermark-free downloads and commercial use, you almost always have to pay.
  
  ### Text-to-Video vs. Image-to-Video: Which is better? +
  
  Image-to-Video wins for control. If you generate an image first (using Midjourney or Flux), you define the exact look, lighting, and composition. Then, the video AI just handles the movement. Text-to-video is faster but more random.
  
  ### Can I use AI-generated videos for commercial ads? +
  
  Generally, yes, if you are on a paid plan. Free plans usually grant a "non-commercial" license. Always double-check the Terms of Service for the specific tool you are using. Rights can vary wildly between platforms.
  
  ### How long can the videos be? +
  
  Direct generation is usually capped between 5 and 10 seconds per clip. However, tools like Kling and Runway allow you to "extend" the clip multiple times. This lets you build continuous shots of up to 2 or 3 minutes if you have the patience (and the credits).
  
